# Data grids. Editability and placement in an expansion panel are two independent properties, so all
# four combinations exist.
#
# A grid has no caption of its own, so its configured label is the caption of the panel that holds
# it. That label is how the grid is found: the framework opens that panel when the grid is not on
# screen yet, and 'check exists' compares the panel caption the same way it compares a field label.

use Supervisor
open UsrTestForm for 71d27c81-3d6b-41d9-9a39-c408c96173b6

click GeneralInfoTab

# Directly on the page, no panel, inline editing on.
check DataGrid_0qy3003 exists
check DataGrid_0qy3003 is editable

# In a panel captioned "Contact Expanded non editable", inline editing off.
check GridDetail_ec8uysl exists
check GridDetail_ec8uysl is not editable

# In a panel captioned "Contact Expanded editable", inline editing on.
check DataGrid_cfoe0pp exists
check DataGrid_cfoe0pp is editable

# Columns are read from the page file, so the assertion covers both the names and their order.
check DataGrid_0qy3003 columns
check GridDetail_ec8uysl columns
check DataGrid_cfoe0pp columns
